ARCHITECTURE WORKFLOW (Simple & Clean)
Developer → Git Push to GitHub
        ↓
GitHub Actions Pipeline
        ├── Step 1: Checkout Code
        ├── Step 2: Build Docker Image
        ├── Step 3: Push to Google Artifact Registry
        └── Step 4: Deploy to Cloud Run
        ↓
Live Cloud Run URL updates automatically


This does NOT require:

No SSH
No VM
No Authorized keys
No Firewall
No Port 22

Everything happens through Google Cloud APIs.

 USE CASE

Deploy a simple Python Flask app to Cloud Run automatically whenever code is pushed to main.

 STEP 1 — Create a simple app (app.py)
from flask import Flask
app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route("/")
def home():
    return "Hello from GitHub Actions + Cloud Run!"

if __name__ == "__main__":
    app.run()

STEP 2 — Create Dockerfile
FROM python:3.9-slim
WORKDIR /app
COPY . .
RUN pip install flask gunicorn
CMD ["gunicorn", "--bind", "0.0.0.0:8080", "app:app"]

 STEP 3 — Push this code to GitHub repo
 STEP 4 — Create GitHub Actions Workflow

Create folder:

mkdir -p .github/workflows


Create file:

.github/workflows/deploy.yml

Paste this:

name: Deploy to Cloud Run

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main

jobs:
  build-deploy:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    permissions:
      contents: read
      id-token: write

    steps:
    - name: Checkout Code
      uses: actions/checkout@v3

    - name: Google Cloud Auth
      uses: google-github-actions/auth@v2
      with:
        credentials_json: ${{ secrets.GCP_SA_KEY }}

    - name: Configure gcloud
      uses: google-github-actions/setup-gcloud@v2

    - name: Build and Push Docker Image
      run: |
        gcloud builds submit --tag gcr.io/${{ secrets.GCP_PROJECT_ID }}/gha-demo-app

    - name: Deploy to Cloud Run
      run: |
        gcloud run deploy gha-demo-app \
        --image gcr.io/${{ secrets.GCP_PROJECT_ID }}/gha-demo-app \
        --region asia-south1 \
        --platform managed \
        --allow-unauthenticated

 STEP 5 — Add the required GitHub secrets

Go to:

GitHub → Repo → Settings → Secrets → Actions

Create these secrets:

 GCP_PROJECT_ID/AWS or Azure


 Service account key

Paste your Service Account JSON key.

To generate:

gcloud iam service-accounts keys create key.json \
   --iam-account=github-actions@testadi-459816.iam.gserviceaccount.com


Grant permissions:

gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding testadi-459816 \
  --member="serviceAccount:github-actions@testadi-459816.iam.gserviceaccount.com" \
  --role="roles/run.admin"

gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding testadi-459816 \
  --member="serviceAccount:github-actions@testadi-459816.iam.gserviceaccount.com" \
  --role="roles/artifactregistry.admin"

gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding testadi-459816 \
  --member="serviceAccount:github-actions@testadi-459816.iam.gserviceaccount.com" \
  --role="roles/cloudbuild.builds.editor"


Upload key.json content to GitHub secret GCP_SA_KEY.

STEP 6 — Push code to GitHub and watch CI/CD run

Whenever you run:

git add .
git commit -m "deploy test"
git push


GitHub Actions will:

✔ Build Docker image
✔ Push to Artifact Registry
✔ Deploy to Cloud Run
✔ Give you a LIVE URL 🚀

 FINAL RESULT

You will get an output like:

Service URL: https://gha-demo-app-abcdef-as.a.run.app




This is the industry standard CI/CD.
